  "what is the difference between a fixed workflow and an agent?|k=8|lectures=": {
   "answer": "The difference between a fixed workflow and an agent is who chooses the next step at runtime [L08 slide 3]. In a fixed workflow, code determines the path, whereas in an agent loop, the model chooses an action, calls a tool, and chooses again using new evidence [L08 slide 3].",
