  "what are the key takeaways of lesson 2?|k=8|lectures=": {
   "answer": "The five key takeaways of Lesson 2 are:\n1. Token counts are model-specific measurements, not word-count estimates [L02 slide 59].\n2. Context must be assembled in order and budgeted before generation [L02 slide 59].\n3. Temperature reshapes a distribution without adding knowledge or truth [L02 slide 59].\n4. Embeddings are model-specific vectors whose geometry depends on an objective [L02 slide 59].\n5. Cosine similarity ranks direction and cannot by itself prove correctness [L02 slide 59].",
